 "hypothesis_card": {
  "mechanism": "The champion's pooled LINEAR momentum OLS cannot represent nonlinear state-conditional dynamics (vol clustering, momentum saturation, sticky zones); the GBM member captures them (alone +0.039 Discovery pooled, the largest single-model gain measured in this lab) but its tree q50 drifts on calm sticky zones in-sample. The 50/50 blend lets the tree carry the pooled gain while the linear member anchors the calm-zone center and the calibrated band. Two bugs were fixed in the archived code: the 4-tuple `per[sid] = (lv, X, y, mask)` unpacked as 5 names (the exact crash) and the undefined `mfall` (should be `m2`). The blend weight was chosen by an OOS dense pseudo-origin backtest (24 origins), not the in-sample dry run: w=0.5 dominates w=0.3 on BOTH axes (pooled +0.0379 vs +0.0254; median 0.2767 v",
  "expected_observation": "On Discovery (11 origins): pooled ~0.481 vs champion 0.446 (+0.035, 10/11 origins), h1 +0.047 / h3 +0.034 / h7 +0.034, coverage ~0.801; in-sample median 0.246 (-0.037) is expected to be leakage. On the dense pseudo-origin backtest (24 origins, stride 3): pooled delta +0.038 (z=6.7, 22/24 origins improved), median 0.277 vs champion 0.281 (-0.0045, inside the Gate-2 tolerance), coverage 0.810. On Holdout: pooled ~0.34-0.36 (Gate-1 threshold 0.3118), median ~0.27-0.28 (Gate-2 floor 0.2695), coverage ~0.75-0.80 (in band), all horizons positive.",
  "competing_explanation": "The rival explanation of the same errors: the +0.038 OOS pooled gain is not the tree's nonlinearity but the GBM's implicit per-series heterogeneity handling (its features include the series' own local vol, so it acts partly as a per-series conditional width model), and the residual median deficit is real tree drift on sticky zones that the backtest's dense pseudo-origins under-weight because they cluster in Aug-Sep where repricing was active. Under this explanation the Holdout median would fall below the Gate-2 floor even though pooled passes, and a linear member with richer per-series features (or a per-series conformal layer on the GBM) would match the blend without any tree.",
  "test": "Dry run on Discovery (11 origins) vs the champion, plus a dense pseudo-origin backtest (24 origins, stride 3) of w_gbm in {0.3, 0.5, 0.7} to select the weight on OOS evidence rather than the in-sample median. The deciding comparison: the committed w=0.5 blend must beat the champion's Discovery pooled 0.4462 (dry run: 0.4814, screen PASS, would_reach_holdout=true) and its OOS median must stay within the Gate-2 tolerance of the champion's (backtest: -0.0045).",
  "rejection_condition": "Falsified if holdout pooled <= 0.3118 (Gate 1), or holdout median < 0.2695 (Gate 2), or coverage leaves [0.74, 0.86] (Gate 3), or any horizon skill < -0.020 (Gate 4). The class-exploration mechanism is additionally falsified if the blend's holdout pooled gain over the champion is below +0.005 (both members' Discovery gains were +0.039 and 0.0; a transfer below +0.005 means the tree gain did not transfer out of sample). The weight-selection method is falsified if the holdout median falls below 0.2695 while pooled passes \u2014 that would mean the OOS backtest median axis also leaks."
